.TH MYFILE_STATS 3 "November 2026" "libmyutils 0.4.1" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
myfile_stats \- count the lines and words in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <myfilefunctions.h>
.sp
.BI "int myfile_stats(const char *" filename ", int *" line_count ", int *" word_count );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B myfile_stats
function opens the file named by
.I filename
and reads it line by line, incrementing
.I *line_count
for every line and accumulating
.I *word_count
using
.BR mywordcount (3)
on each line. Together these give a
.BR wc (1)
-style summary of the file.
.PP
All three parameters are required;
.B NULL
in any of
.IR filename ,
.IR line_count ,
or
.I word_count
causes the function to fail immediately.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, with
.I *line_count
and
.I *word_count
populated.
Returns \-1 if any argument is
.B NULL
or the file could not be opened.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <myfilefunctions.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    int lines, words;
    if (myfile_stats("notes.txt", &lines, &words) == 0)
        printf("%d lines, %d words\en", lines, words);
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Written as part of the OS Assignment 01: Core C Utilities Library.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wc (1),
.BR mywordcount (3)
